# LaughTail SMP - .gitignore
# Spec 33.3 step 2: this file must exist and be correct BEFORE the first commit.
# A secret committed once lives in history forever, even after deletion.
# Never-break rule 5 (AGENTS.md): never commit a secret.

# --- Required minimum set, verbatim from spec 33.3 ---
.env
*.env
docs/private/
*.key
*.pem
id_rsa*
*.sql
backups/
logs/
world*/
*.log

# --- Carve-out: see docs/decisions.md D-0001 and docs/questions.md Q-01 ---
# Spec 33.3 excludes *.sql, but the same section's tree requires db/migrations/
# and Appendix D defines a schema that must be version-controlled.
# Schema migrations are code, not data, and contain no secrets.
!db/migrations/
!db/migrations/**/*.sql

# --- Additional exclusions (spec 33.3 says "at minimum") ---
# Local connection details. Acceptance row 2: no IP addresses or absolute host
# paths anywhere in the repository. The committed template is host.env.example.ps1.
scripts/host.env.ps1

# Local artefact cache written by scripts/verify-manifest.ps1. Jars are pinned
# in server/manifest.yml with publisher checksums; they are never committed.
.cache/

*.jar
*.jar.sha256.tmp
*.p12
*.pfx
*.ppk
id_ed25519*
*.kdbx
credentials*
secrets*
*.dump
*.bak

# Paper / Pelican runtime artefacts that must never enter git (Section 29:
# the repository is the source of truth for CONFIG, not for runtime state)
server/**/cache/
server/**/libraries/
server/**/versions/
server/**/plugins/**/*.db
server/**/plugins/**/data/
server/**/crash-reports/
server/**/banned-*.json
server/**/ops.json
server/**/usercache.json
server/**/session.lock
server/**/eula.txt
*.mca
*.mcr

# OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
